AUDIT_REPORT.md flagged this as missing (Medium): "every list (clients,
campaigns) renders unpaginated and unsorted." Both are server-rendered,
no client JS, following the same plain-GET-links pattern as the existing
date range picker and clients search/filter.

Clients list: added a sort dropdown (name A-Z/Z-A, revenue high-low) and
12-per-page pagination. Sorting by name only fetches live Shopify revenue
for the current page's clients rather than every client, unlike sorting
by revenue which necessarily needs every filtered client's totals first
to sort correctly — a real efficiency win for the common case, not just
pagination for its own sake.

Campaign table (shared across Meta/Google/TikTok, the admin dashboard,
client portal, and public share links): column headers for Campaign,
Spend, Revenue, ROAS, Purchases, Impressions, and Clicks are now click-
to-sort links (toggling direction on repeat clicks), plus 25-per-page
pagination. resolveCampaignTableParams() is exported from channel-page.tsx
and reused by every caller that resolves raw searchParams (AdsChannelPage
and the three client-portal ads pages route through it; the public share
page calls it directly).

Deliberately scoped to the two lists the audit names explicitly. The
newer ad set/ad/keyword/audience/product breakdown tables added earlier
this pass already cap-and-sort-by-spend server-side, which covers the
same "unbounded table" risk without retrofitting full pagination onto
every one of them too.

